    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm looking for some help with a tax question. my family is dealing with an estate that has properties in both the uk and spain, plus some offshore accounts. i need to understand how inheritance tax works when assets are spread out like this and what the main residency rules are for the beneficiaries. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the deceased was likely subject to UK Inheritance Tax only if domiciled in the UK at the time of death, assets in Spain and offshore accounts may be subject to different taxes depending on the beneficiary's residency rather than the asset location alone for the UK estate. For heirs becoming residents in Spain, they will generally only pay Spanish Inheritance Tax on Spanish assets and those mandate bases required by local law, but they must track residency changes carefully as this affects UK tax liabilities. It is strongly advisable to consult with both UK and Spanish tax professionals to navigate the dual-residency complexities and specific threshold rules for each jurisdiction.",
